Native macOS uses the operating system's Apple NFS client/server; they are not
redistributed inside the control binary.

Linux uses Ubuntu Noble NFS-Ganesha4.3-8ubuntu1 sources and distro patches/rules,
with accepted upstream98eb77c4fd94effa6882b214698a77752ec79f6e's two-field
GET_DIR_DELEGATION correction, packaged as4.3-8ubuntu1+autobyteus1. Upstream fix:
Suhas Athani; see packaging/engine/get-dir-delegation.patch for provenance.
Ganesha/VFS retain LGPL-3.0-or-later and their component licenses. nfs-common
retains GPL-2.0-or-later and its component licenses. The .deb pair is embedded
as package data in Linux CLIs, not statically linked into Go. Package copyright
records are appended to the Linux archive notices and retained in the image.

Every engine candidate carries its full corresponding modified Debian source,
including the original tar, modified Debian delta, dsc, exact patch/build recipe
and copyright. Versioned autobyteus-nfs-ganesha-source-<version>-<arch>.tar.gz
artifacts accompany authorized publication. The engine manifest records exact
source/package/recipe hashes; do not substitute prototype or stock package bytes.
The image records the same manifest and package inventory under
/usr/share/autobyteus-nfs/. Stock distro runtime dependencies retain source
availability through the recorded Ubuntu package versions and archive.

The Ubuntu base image and package dependencies retain their respective
licenses and notices. Release evidence records its immutable digest; do not
represent AutoByteus's license as relicensing those operating-system packages.
